{% extends '@UhifadhiDevkit/console/base.html.twig' %}
{% import '@UhifadhiDevkit/console/_parts.html.twig' as parts %}

{% set devkit_tab = 'commands' %}

{% block title %}Commands{% endblock %}
{% block shell_page_title %}Commands{% endblock %}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}
    The assembled dev commands and seed-content loaders the fleet contributes.
    Every module ships <b>inert provider classes</b> that declare its commands
    through the contracts (<code class="mono">Devkit\CommandProviderInterface</code>,
    <code class="mono">Devkit\ContentProviderInterface</code>); devkit collects
    them into the one list below &mdash; a single place to find everything the
    fleet contributes, without grepping ten <code class="mono">composer.json</code>
    files. In v1 the commands run from the CLI; this surface reads and assembles them.
{% endblock %}

{% block devkit_content %}
    <div class="grid g4" style="margin-bottom:26px">
        <div class="c"><span class="tab">assembled</span><div class="kpi"><b>{{ catalogue.total }}</b><div class="sub">commands &middot; from {{ catalogue.contributorCount }} modules</div></div></div>
        <div class="c"><span class="tab">seed content</span><div class="kpi"><b>{{ catalogue.seedContentCount }}</b><div class="sub">seed:seed loaders</div></div></div>
        <div class="c"><span class="tab">deprecated</span><div class="kpi"><b>{{ catalogue.deprecatedCount }}</b><div class="sub">dying commands</div></div></div>
        <div class="c"><span class="tab">contributors</span><div class="kpi"><b>{{ catalogue.contributorCount }}</b><div class="sub">modules ship commands</div></div></div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="zone">The assembled command list &mdash; grouped by contributing module</h2>

    {% for group in catalogue.groups %}{{ parts.group(group) }}{% endfor %}

    <div class="dk-note" style="margin-top:24px"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4"/><path d="M12 8h.01"/></svg><div class="bd"><b>Why the Run buttons are disabled.</b> v1 is an <b>inspector</b> console &mdash; commands run from the CLI, and this surface reads and assembles them so a builder can discover what the whole fleet contributes. A web command-runner and scaffolding are a later phase; the affordance is drawn here, deliberately inert.</div></div>

    <div class="dk-note"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4"/><path d="M12 8h.01"/></svg><div class="bd"><b>Deprecation is a flagged gap.</b> Neither devkit contract carries a deprecation signal, so the console cannot mark a dying command without guessing from its name. Marking one needs a <code class="mono">deprecated</code> flag on the descriptor contract &mdash; an owner decision.</div></div>
{% endblock %}
